  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">China FIT: Strengthening Capacity for World Heritage in AFR and APA regions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project strengthens the identification, nomination, conservation and promotion of cultural and natural heritage in Africa and Asia-Pacific, particularly Small Island Developing States (SIDS), through capacity-building, technical support and South-South cooperation with China. It will support at least four African countries in preparing nomination dossiers, while assisting SIDS to update Tentative Lists, prepare Preliminary Assessment requests and reinforce national heritage systems. The project advances SDG 11.4 and regional agendas by enhancing the representation, sustainability and resilience of heritage systems in Africa and Asia-Pacific.</narrative>
  </description>
